 # Changelog
 
+## 0.7.10 — 2026-11-13
+
+Spool 0.7.10 clarifies how ownership transfer works in a local owner session and how to recover a pending invitation that has no saved link.
+
+### What you can now do
+
+- **Understand how to confirm a local ownership transfer.** Members explains that an owner session opened through this copy's local access link confirms the transfer with local access. The member's Manage access panel points to Confirm owner transfer. Other sessions still require identity verification; local development does not send verification email.
+- **Recover a pending invitation with no saved link.** Members explains how to remove the pending member through Manage access and invite that address again. Trying to invite an already-pending address gives the same recovery steps. A new local invitation has its own single-use, expiring link for that machine.
+
+### Updating
+
+Back up first: download a private archive in Settings, or stop local dev and run `rer export --output exports/spool.jsonl`. From 0.7.9 on main, update with `git pull --ff-only` and `rer dev`; from a tag, run `git fetch --tags && git checkout v0.7.10` and `rer dev`. For a hosted installation, use `rer deploy` from the original deploying checkout. Keep the database, private settings, project keys and deployment receipt. There are no new migrations or breaking changes after 0.7.9; previously applied migration files are unchanged, so do not reset. Import private archives only into an empty destination. The application still pins rer exactly to 0.2.107. This application release does not publish the Spool SDK.
+
+### Known limits
+
+- Local development sends no email. Email verification for ownership transfer remains unavailable there; only an owner session opened through the local access link uses local confirmation.
+- Browser restore is limited to 16 MiB. Larger current JSONL archives need the CLI; legacy JSON archives over 16 MiB remain refused. A refused legacy JSON upload over 16 MiB can still end in a connection reset: the fix drains only what the restore engine has not already begun reading. Refused requests on the agent-door `/mcp` route are not covered by this fix.
+- Agent setup still requires an owner to save all six policy answers and create a project agent key. The agent CLI runs from a Spool checkout; it is not an npm-published package. Local agent calls also require the private dev gate described in the panel.
+- Erasing the owner is held while other stored agent text contains a different address that ends with the owner's address. The erasure match is case-sensitive.
+- Before the first project is created, opening a missing project URL as the owner redirects to setup instead of showing a not-found page.
+- Retained hosted archives still require separate Managed-to-native release qualification. If an archive is refused with `schema_mismatch`, restore into the release you exported from. Retrying a cut-off hosted restore can be refused until its five-minute lease expires; wait before retrying.
+- Bugsnag, Rollbar and Sentry imports remain bounded to 2 MiB and 500 records; larger sets are refused rather than partly applied. A real-account migration and live mail delivery through Cloudflare remain unqualified.
+
+Product screenshot: .github/assets/release/spool-issue-page-1600.png
+
 ## 0.7.9 — 2026-11-13
 
 Spool 0.7.9 clarifies capture setup, missing release information and locally suppressed email, and explains what Slack and cron forwarding need before you connect them.
